    "body": "## Problem\n\nLSP requires Markdown to follow the [GFM spec](https://github.github.com/gfm/#backslash-escapes), where any ASCII punctuation character may be backslash-escaped. Servers escape `.`, `_` and `-` in prose to avoid accidental list or emphasis parsing, but `_normalize_markdown()` never resolves those escapes, so hover shows them:\n\n```\nReturns the sum\\. See also `Foo\\_Bar`\\-baz\\.\n```\n\nFixes #41910\n\n## Solution\n\nResolve backslash escapes as a fourth normalization step:\n\n```\nReturns the sum. See also `Foo\\_Bar`-baz.\n```\n\nIt runs after thematic breaks are expanded, so an escaped `\\---` is not turned into a divider. Code spans and fenced code blocks stay verbatim, since a backslash is literal there — hence `Foo\\_Bar` above is unchanged. An escaped backtick does not open a code span.\n\n## Validation\n\n`TEST_FILE=test/functional/plugin/lsp/util_spec.lua make functionaltest`: 67 passed, including two new cases. `lsp_spec.lua` and the remaining `plugin/lsp/` specs: 429 passed. `make lintlua`, `make emmylua-check` and `make lintcommit` clean. macOS arm64.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-22T17:06:55Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am genuinely grateful for your interest in making Nvim better. However, this looks like a low-effort AI contribution, and we don't need those.\r\n\r\nPlease review [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md).\r\n\r\nBecause of the volume of AI PRs, we will block users with no warning if PRs do not show evidence of:\r\n\r\n1. Clueful review of CONTRIBUTING.md\r\n2. Human effort put into the decisions of the proposed change.\r\n    - This especially implies finding ways to make the reviewer's job easier. That often means \"less is more\", but also just the right amount, of code, docs, PR comments, PR desc., etc.",
